course: dictionary
lesson: 5890
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Mantle is a good example. In science, the mantle is a thick, hot layer of rock inside the Earth. «Under the Earth's thin rocky crust lies the mantle, hot rock that is solid but flows very slowly.»
explain: In stories, a mantle can be a loose cloak, or a duty that passes from one person to another. When you read «take on the mantle», the words take on tell you it means an important role. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The Earth has a thin rocky crust, a thick hot mantle and a very hot core in the middle.» Crust and core are both layers of the Earth, so the mantle must be a layer too, the one between them.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If the Earth's mantle were a cloak, the sentence would make no sense. When the clues are not enough, use a dictionary.
fact: A mantle is a thick, hot layer of rock inside the Earth, between the crust and the core.
fact: The mantle is solid but flows very slowly, and the plates of the crust ride on it.
fact: «Take on the mantle» means to accept an important duty or role that has passed to you.
fact: «A mantle of snow» means a covering of snow, like a cloak spread over the ground.
fact: Long ago, a mantle was a loose cloak without sleeves.
exercise: «Under the Earth's thin rocky crust lies the mantle.» Where is the mantle? | At the bottom of the sea only | Inside a tree | *Between the crust and the core | In the sky above the clouds
exercise: «She was asked to take on the mantle of team captain.» What does mantle mean here? | A thick layer of rock | A covering of snow | *A role or duty passed on to her | A loose cloak without sleeves
exercise: «The hills wore a mantle of snow.» What does mantle mean here? | *A covering, like a cloak over the ground | A hot layer deep inside the Earth | A bird that lives in the hills | A sharp, jagged rock
test: In «The Earth has a thin rocky crust, a thick hot mantle and a very hot core», which layer lies between the crust and the core? | Volcano | Core | *Mantle | Crust
test: «Diamond is pure carbon squeezed deep in the mantle, about 150 km down.» Where was the diamond formed? | On top of a mountain | *Deep in the mantle, about 150 km down | In the sea, under the waves | Near the surface, under a tree
exam: Which clue best tells you that mantle means a layer of the Earth? | The word thick, which only tells you about size | Nothing, you must look it up in a dictionary | The word and, which joins two things | *Crust and core, which are both layers of the Earth
